<messaging:emailTemplate relatedToType="Account"    subject="ACCOUNT OWNER AR:   Audit Starts Today.   Completion due {!$Label.Core_Account_Team_Adudit_Due_date} !">
    <messaging:htmlEmailBody > 
        <html>  
            <body>  
                 <p>Dear {!relatedTo.Owner.Name},</p>
                
                     <p>As the Owner of one or more Accounts, Internal Audit requires that you review Account Team Members
                        and their access levels on Accounts, Opportunities and Cases. This provides assurance that access has
                        been limited to the Team Members who are working on an Account.  It is important that you remove
                        Team Members who are no longer working on your accounts.   Please reference the <a href="https://salescrm.intel.com/account-review-audit-2019/" target="_blank">audit
                        communication sent {!$Label.Core_Account_Team_Audit_Communication_date} </a> for more details and guidance </p>
                        <p>
                        <apex:outputlink value="{!LEFT($Api.Partner_Server_URL_140,FIND('.com',$Api.Partner_Server_URL_140)+4)+'lightning/n/core_account_team_review'}">
                            Visit this page to review your Accounts' Team Members by {!$Label.Core_Account_Team_Adudit_Due_date}, {!YEAR( TODAY() )} 
                         </apex:outputlink>
                         </p>
                      <p>For Team Members who belong on the Account Team, you should set the Account, Opportunity and
                         Case access level (Private, Read, or Read/Write) to the appropriate "need to know" level. Note that
                         Account Read/Write access grants Team Members the ability to edit Contact information and to
                         emulate customers who are IPS Active Contacts. In addition, it provides edit access to non-core Account
                         fields   
                      </p>
                      <p>
                         Please visit the linked page containing all the Accounts and Team Members that currently require your
                         review. For each account, when your review and updates are complete, mark the Review Completed
                         box, and make sure to save your change.    
                      </p>
                      <p><b>This review must be completed by {!$Label.Core_Account_Team_Adudit_Due_date}, {!YEAR( TODAY() )}.</b>For questions or further information, please log an 
                          <apex:outputlink value="{!LEFT($Api.Partner_Server_URL_140,FIND('.com',$Api.Partner_Server_URL_140)+4)+'lightning/n/ask_a_question'}">
                            Ask a Question (AAQ). 
                         </apex:outputlink>
                      </p>
                  <p>Thank you!</p> 

            </body>    

        </html>  
        </messaging:htmlEmailBody>
                  
</messaging:emailTemplate>